expl('EXP067','INC130;INC131;INC132;INC133','Helicopter or other conventional aircraft (hovering, rotor-like sound, running lights, lights off over the WSA) as stated in the NORAD and message traffic; Wurtsmith: no aircraft identified, Michigan DNR had none up. For INC132 and INC133: memory conflation with INC131 (Erikson, 20 years later) and bright planet or aircraft light misjudged at night (Dunn, 30 years later). No evidence found here to test any of these.','NORAD log and 11 Nov 1975 CINCNORAD message use the word helicopter; Wurtsmith witnesses heard helicopter-like sound; Taylor estimates are rough.','Taylor reports speed ~1000 kt and 200 kt chase by estimate; radar paint ~10 s; no helicopter identified; DNR denial reported by Clear Intent only; Eichner object not helicopter.','OPEN',14607)
src('SRC071','Wurtsmith AFB Incursion (NCP summary, incl. NORAD log extract)','Francis Ridge (NICAP/NCP)','NICAP','2006-03-15','Web case summary','SECONDARY','https://nicap.org/babylon/751030_wurtsmith.htm','','whole page',A,'INC131;CLM267;CLM269','Names the NORAD entry 31 Oct 75 0445Z for incident at 0355Z, helicopter hovered over SAC WSA, tanker visual + skin paint, object tracked 25 NM SE over Lake Huron; says FBI Saginaw and police notified, DNR contacted, never explained. Cites Good, Fawcett and Greenwood, Stone.','Secondary compilation of a FOIA release; do not treat as the original log.','PARTIALLY_VERIFIED','EXAMINED')
src('SRC072','Clear Intent chapter "Wurtsmith and Others" (excerpt), 1984','Lawrence Fawcett and Barry Greenwood','NICAP (reposted 2007)','2007-06-06','Book chapter excerpt','SECONDARY','https://nicap.org/articles/CI-Wurtsmith.htm','','pp. 41-56',A,'INC130;INC131;CLM265;CLM267;CLM268;CLM269','Gives SP/KC-135 names, Taylor Memo for the Record of 18 Jan 1979, wing historian Cahill research log, and the CINCNORAD message of 11 Nov 1975 describing Loring and Wurtsmith objects as helicopters. Says Taylor never called the craft a helicopter. Quotes Taylor: speed ~200 kt, 1 mile off, 1000 kt recession; radar paint 10 s.','Secondary but quotes released documents at length; originals not seen.','PARTIALLY_VERIFIED','EXAMINED')
ev('EVD137',"The Wurtsmith 30 Oct 1975 case rests on released AF documents quoted in Clear Intent: SP statements, a NORAD log entry, a CINCNORAD message, and a Taylor memo written 18 Jan 1979. The log and message say helicopter; Taylor and the SPs do not. Taylor dates it 'around the 1st of November', 3 days later than the log. Original documents not seen here.",'GOVERNMENT_RECORD','SRC071; SRC072; book 14607-14650','INC131;CLM267;CLM268;CLM269',14607,'HIGH','PARTIALLY_VERIFIED')
ev('EVD138',"Malmstrom WSA 1975: no document, only Chassey's rumor and Peisher's agreement. Peisher's timeline conflict with Chassey's separation date is noted by Hastings. A separate Nov 1975 Malmstrom event (radar 7 kt, F-106 scramble) in the CINCNORAD message is not this event.",'ANALYST_ASSESSMENT','book 14254-14483; SRC072','INC128;CLM261;CLM262',14301,'MEDIUM','UNVERIFIED')
